Regenerate three stale pytest-regressions fixtures

The already-staged fixture migration off `aiida.manage.tests.pytest_fixtures`
moved this suite from `core.psql_dos` (PostgreSQL, whose `jsonb` column
reorders an object's keys by byte length and then lexicographically) to
`core.sqlite_dos` (plain JSON, which echoes back whatever order the dict was
built in).  `_write_input_file` in aiida_orca/calculations/orca_orca.py does
nothing more than `params = parameters.get_dict()` and write each
`input_blocks` entry in that order, so these three recorded fixtures — all
written against the old psql-jsonb key order — are simply stale.  Same
category of staleness as the `pbc1`/`pbc2`/`pbc3` fix in
../aiida-quantumespresso/default.nix, and `--force-regen` is the wrong tool
here for the same reason given there: it would also paper over a genuinely
wrong fixture anywhere else in the suite.

